From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:46:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/44] qwen27: YaRN rope, SenseNova-Loop registration and a
 shared loop schedule

The 27B Metal engine refused every scaled rope by design. It now reads
rope_parameters' YaRN type with factor and original_max_position_embeddings,
builds transformers' static table in core/rope_yarn.zig and passes it to
q27_rope as 32 frequencies plus the attention factor that cos and sin carry;
every other scaling, a legacy rope_scaling block, a beta other than 32/1 and
truncate: false stay refused by name.

core/loop_schedule.zig reads loop_settings into an execution plan shared by
every backend: physical layer and per-kind mixer slot per execution, plus the
mHC range with its streams, iterations and phase-boundary rule. The released
SenseNova-Loop-9B plan is 56 executions from 32 layers.

metal.zig registers sensenova_loop alongside qwen3_5 on the dense 9B geometry
that model.zig already admitted.
